From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] viogpu_umd: AV1 film grain, interlaced H.264, exact multi-tile AV1

D3D12 video decoding, on top of the decoder (0004): ffmpeg's d3d12va now
decodes every test clip bit-exact against libavcodec/libdav1d (H.264
progressive, MBAFF, field pictures and mixed; HEVC Main/Main 10/4K; VP9 8/10;
AV1 8/10-bit, 1080p with tiles, film grain 8/10-bit).

- AV1: inline session parameters (VK_KHR_video_maintenance2, enabled by
  vkd3d-proton where the device has it): NVIDIA's decoder takes a sequence
  header from a parameters object differently from the same one passed with
  the decode; a 4-tile 8-bit clip came out with chroma off by one here and
  there. Every decode parameter, the bitstream layout, images and session
  were compared with ffmpeg's Vulkan decoder (bit-exact on the same GPU): the
  parameters object was the one difference. refresh_frame_flags (not in
  DXVA) turned out not to matter.
- AV1 film grain: the profile with film grain support; a picture that applies
  grain decodes out of place, into one more image after the DPB slots', and
  that is what lands in the application's texture, while its DPB picture
  stays without grain for the pictures that reference it (as ffmpeg's Vulkan
  decoder does with NVIDIA's coinciding DPB and output). DXVA's grain
  parameters are the picture's as they apply, so update_grain is always set.
- AV1 loop restoration unit sizes for every plane whenever one restores.
- Interlaced H.264: streams that aren't frames-only get the interleaved
  picture layout; field pictures decode into one slot per frame (the second
  field into the first's), the setup and references carry the fields decoded
  (field-coded references only, as ffmpeg's Vulkan decoder has them), the
  first field of a pair is a complementary field pair, and a second field
  that references its first doesn't bind its slot twice.
- HEVC encoding caps: minimum coding unit 16x16 (the encoder's is 8x8):
  applications pad reconstructed pictures to it, and a decoder's 1088-line
  frames then match them (ffmpeg's hevc_d3d12va fed straight from d3d12va at
  1080p failed the runtime's reference size check).
---
diff --git a/libs/viogpu_umd/umd_video.cpp b/libs/viogpu_umd/umd_video.cpp
index 96cbd7af..6f984933 100644
--- a/libs/viogpu_umd/umd_video.cpp
+++ b/libs/viogpu_umd/umd_video.cpp
@@ -86,6 +86,11 @@ video_get(viogpu_device *device)
    if (video->family == VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED && video->decodeFamily == VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_IGNORED)
       return NULL;
    video->GetPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties(video->physical, &video->memory);
+   VkPhysicalDeviceVideoMaintenance2FeaturesKHR maintenance2 = {
+      VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_VIDEO_MAINTENANCE_2_FEATURES_KHR};
+   VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures2 features = {VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_FEATURES_2, &maintenance2};
+   video->GetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2(video->physical, &features);
+   video->maintenance2 = maintenance2.videoMaintenance2;
    video->ok = true;
    viogpu_log("video: encoding on queue family %d, decoding on %d", (int)video->family, (int)video->decodeFamily);
    return video;
@@ -509,9 +514,11 @@ video_get_caps_(D3D12DDI_HDEVICE hDevice, const D3D12DDIARG_VIDEO_GETCAPS_0020 *
             s->SupportFlags |=
                D3D12DDI_VIDEO_ENCODER_CODEC_CONFIGURATION_SUPPORT_HEVC_FLAG_0083_0_ASYMETRIC_MOTION_PARTITION_SUPPORT |
                D3D12DDI_VIDEO_ENCODER_CODEC_CONFIGURATION_SUPPORT_HEVC_FLAG_0083_0_ASYMETRIC_MOTION_PARTITION_REQUIRED;
-         /* coding units 8x8 up to the CTB, transform units 4x4 up to 32x32, the full hierarchy */
+         /* coding units 16x16 up to the CTB, transform units 4x4 up to 32x32, the full hierarchy. 16, not the
+          * encoder's 8: applications pad their reconstructed pictures to it (ffmpeg's hevc_d3d12va does), and
+          * decoders' 1088-line frames then match them (with 8, 1080p from a decoder fails the runtime's check) */
          UINT ctb = block_size(c, true);
-         s->MinLumaCodingUnitSize = D3D12DDI_VIDEO_ENCODER_CODEC_CONFIGURATION_HEVC_0080_CUSIZE_8x8;
+         s->MinLumaCodingUnitSize = D3D12DDI_VIDEO_ENCODER_CODEC_CONFIGURATION_HEVC_0080_CUSIZE_16x16;
          s->MaxLumaCodingUnitSize = (D3D12DDI_VIDEO_ENCODER_CODEC_CONFIGURATION_HEVC_CUSIZE_0080)(log2_of(ctb) - 3);
          s->MinLumaTransformUnitSize = D3D12DDI_VIDEO_ENCODER_CODEC_CONFIGURATION_HEVC_TUSIZE_0082_0_4x4;
          s->MaxLumaTransformUnitSize = D3D12DDI_VIDEO_ENCODER_CODEC_CONFIGURATION_HEVC_TUSIZE_0082_0_32x32;
